Package: theoryforge
Title: Systematic Theory Development
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Pablo", family = "Bernabeu", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "pcbernabeu@gmail.com", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1083-2460"))
Description: Helps researchers state scientific theories as structured,
    versioned files of constructs, propositions, predictions, rival accounts
    and test records. Functions read and validate these files, check how
    completely a theory is specified against a versioned checklist, screen
    constructs for overlapping definitions, derive the conditional
    independence relations and the signs of effects that a theory's causal
    graph implies, compare a theory with a rival or with an earlier version
    of itself, compile 'lavaan' model syntax, simulate the construct network
    as a linear system, write the theory and hypotheses sections of a
    preregistration and a dossier for reviewers, record the outcomes of
    tests, map a theory onto the themes of a literature corpus and draw
    diagrams of it. A 'Python' package of the same name offers the same
    functions. Both follow one specification, so they give the same results
    and the same diagrams for the same file and settings.
